From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: K230 Yocto <k230-yocto@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 16:48:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lib: sbi: skip unusable single-entry PMP protection

The local K230 QEMU model exposes one PMP entry. OpenSBI 1.8 registers
PMP-based hart protection whenever any PMP entry exists, but a single entry
cannot encode the generic root domain's firmware and S/U memory regions.
That makes cold boot stop with "insufficient PMP entries".

Treat a single PMP entry as unusable for hart protection. This keeps the
boot path equivalent to a platform without usable PMP support.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local K230 QEMU model workaround]

Signed-off-by: K230 Yocto <k230-yocto@example.invalid>
---
 lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart_pmp.c
@@ -324,6 +324,14 @@ static struct sbi_hart_protection epmp_protection = {
 int sbi_hart_pmp_init(struct sbi_scratch *scratch)
 {
 	int rc;
+
+	/*
+	 * A single PMP entry is not enough to describe the OpenSBI root
+	 * domain's firmware and S/U memory regions. Registering hart
+	 * protection in that case makes boot fail during PMP configuration.
+	 */
+	if (sbi_hart_pmp_count(scratch) <= 1)
+		return 0;
 
 	if (sbi_hart_pmp_count(scratch)) {
 		if (sbi_hart_has_extension(scratch, SBI_HART_EXT_SMEPMP)) {
-- 
